{"availability":"available","full":"error-try-again/QRGen","name":"QRGen","description":"Full-Stack QR Code generation service for self-hosting","category":"Developer tools","language":"Shell","stars":81,"forks":4,"created":"2023-10-06T01:57:11Z","updated":"2024-05-07T15:53:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://qr-gen.net","topics":["express","foss","fullstack","qr","react","scaling","service","ts","vite"],"demo":"https://qr-gen.net/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.389Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.389Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.389Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.389Z","stars":81,"forks":4}],"technologies":["React","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project aims to automate the setup of a scalable, self-hostable, full-stack QR code generation service within a rootless Docker environment, with a focus on security & ease of use. The project has been written in TS (Express), TSX (Vite/React), Bash/Shell (Automation) and has several key layers. Each of which deserve their own companion documentation. To address the challenge of supporting multiple stack configurations, the project has gone through several iterations since its inception. Currently, it is comprised of two separate git submodules that are initialized within the containers…","Note: If you're looking for a version of this project that does not use submodules and instead copies sources from the host/docker-primary user, see the legacy branch.","The first submodule is an optional backend (Express) which provides an operational mode where QR codes are generated on the server. This is a complex design decision and is in preparation for a full-release version of the application, which will support several additional features such as link shortening/dynamic linking, QR code generation history, administrative configuration, user accounts/auth. This decision aims to provide an additional layer of security to the generation process, preventing certain types of speculative malicious QR injection & redirection attacks. To read more about…"],"features":["QRGen supports the the QR Code generation in the following formats for both bulk and regular code generation","Digital Contact Cards","Google Reviews (user provided API key)","Dark mode, responsive, and mobile/tablet friendly design with a focus on accessibility and usability.","Self-hostable QR code generation"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/error-try-again/QRGen/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"73a3b038473b37e8dcab1a2a982a661c876873e68f91815c982376655b408f6c","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.512Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.512Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project aims to automate the setup of a scalable, self-hostable, full-stack QR code generation service within a rootless Docker environment, with a focus on security & ease of use. The project has been written in TS (Express), TSX (Vite/React), Bash/Shell (Automation) and has several key layers. Each of which deserve their own companion documentation. To address the challenge of supporting multiple stack configurations, the project has gone through several iterations since its inception. Currently, it is comprised of two separate git submodules that are initialized within the containers…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/error-try-again/QRGen/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"With keys, without ssh root-login, run the dependency installation script","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/error-try-again/QRGen/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"73a3b038473b37e8dcab1a2a982a661c876873e68f91815c982376655b408f6c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/error-try-again/QRGen/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:23.513Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-05-07T15:53:03Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com